Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 12:17:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 28/71] Keep the prompt cache warm while a tool call runs

The idle refresh budget prices the chance that a paused session has been
abandoned, and stops after five refreshes. A build or a test suite is not that
case: it routinely outlasts the cache TTL several times over, and the request
carrying its output is already scheduled, so the refresh is certain to be
claimed. Tool dispatch now holds the budget open for its duration, released by
a guard so a failed or cancelled call cannot leak the suspension.
---
 codex-rs/core/src/client.rs                  |  9 +++
 codex-rs/core/src/prompt_cache_keep_alive.rs | 70 +++++++++++++++++++-
 codex-rs/core/src/tools/router.rs            |  6 ++
 3 files changed, 83 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

